<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE January wheat up A$1.50/tn in light trade.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE January wheat up A$1.50/tn in light trade.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Another day of light trading left nearby January wheat A$1.50 higher at A$160.00 a tonne on volume of 20 lots at the Sydney Futures Exchange</p>
<p>Traders said January edged higher on overnight sentiment in the U.S., where CBOT wheat closed one to 5-1/2 U.S cents higher.</p>
<p>In the lead-up to the holiday season, traders said they were expecting little increase in volume trading, given only patchy interest was being shown at present from growers.  </p>
